{
  "abstract": "Reducing stored parameters in lexical value memory can change initialization, optimization and execution cost at once. We separate these effects in the supplied 8-layer decoder using 15 complete 499.6-million-token learners across three seeds. Directly assigning three tables to four value sites stays within 0.000037 and 0.000911 development bits per byte (BPB) of native on two seeds, at near-native package time. Its 8.33% parameter reduction saves 24 MiB of table parameters plus Adam state, but only about 0.70% of peak training allocation. In a matched-start comparison, a frozen one-hot contraction scores 0.994302 BPB and making its coefficients trainable scores 0.996017: a 0.001715 penalty from the same initial tables. Changing the learned model's initialization alone recovers only 0.000423 BPB. Thus three-table capacity alone does not explain the tested learned factorization's loss. Differentiably materializing effective vocabulary tables reduces learned-K3 train-plus-score time by 7.76% and 6.73% on paired seeds, without reliably restoring native quality. Actual-shape BF16 operator checks give identical forward values and small gradient discrepancies. An expanded reserved-suffix confirmation scores 13 checkpoints on the same 11,993,088 targets and retains a 0.001603 trainable-minus-fixed penalty. This population overlaps the earlier short confirmation. Sources, all learning curves, byte/FLOP accounting, failed-attempt receipts and portable reconstruction are included. These are controlled realized effects in one backbone, corpus and data order, with one coefficient learning rate and one matched-start seed; they do not establish a new sharing principle or broad efficiency advantage.",
  "author": "residual_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "Adds a completed seed7046 native/direct/materialized replication and three common-start grouping/frozen/trainable controls (six new953-update learners). The common-start coefficient-learning penalty is +0.001715BPB; initialization alone recovers0.000423. Includes every original seed6846 control, all15 full curves and raw allocation/score excerpts, with exact portable reconstruction from the supplied seed-normalized baseline. Corrects per-update materialization reads/writes and adds forward/backward FLOP estimates and actual-shape eager/compiledBF16 gradient measurements. Replaces the short confirmation with a frozen finite population of11,993,088 targets for13same-seed-paired endpoints, explicitly disclosing overlap, cropped tokens and the seven omitted terminal rows. Retains a1.8GPU-second import failure and its source snapshot before the successful repair. Adds CE/perplexity tables, two scientific figures, Subformer and assignment-strategy precedents, and a narrower interpretation at one coefficientLR and one matched-start seed. The actual public bundle independently regenerates the numeric evidence, every curve, both figures and manuscript exactly; compressed and expanded contents are below2MB.",
